    "speaker": "client",
    "text": "Salam Jonas,\n\nPlease let me know what you think about this first round of customer feedback, which I have grouped by issue below.\n\nField behavior and text entry:\n• Proposal (Indstilling) placeholder fields: Unlike in the Executive Summary, clicking the \"insert\" fields—Advantages, settings, attachments, headline, and date—does not automatically clear the existing text.\n• Guidance (Vejledning) reflections: Under \"(write own reflections, if any),\" the placeholder text has the same failure to clear automatically as in the Proposal fields.\n• Board Seminar (Bestyrelsesseminar) agenda: The \"(insert agenda)\" field has the same automatic-clearing issue as the Proposal fields.\n• Proposal text boxes: When the boxes on the left, including the headline, run out of room, words do not wrap automatically. The right-hand column is pushed farther to the right instead.\n• Proposal line breaks: Because automatic wrapping is missing, users are forced to insert line breaks manually. A normal line break (hard return) creates excessive spacing for continuous text, even though that spacing works well between bullet points. A soft return (Shift\\+Enter) gives the correct result, but I doubt our colleagues know how to use it.\n• Board Seminar multi-line support: Under \"Item and Title,\" users must be able to enter multiple lines, including through manual line breaks.\n\nLayout and formatting:\n• Guidance margins: The margins beneath the \"(short description)\" section are not fixed. Without manual line breaks, the \"pencil\" icon is gradually cut off. Can fixed margins be set there?\n• Guidance theme description: This has the same hard-return spacing problem as the Proposal.\n• Board Meeting (Bestyrelsesmøde) alignment: Compared with \"Topic,\" \"Proposal,\" and \"Start time,\" \"Item and Title\" is not aligned correctly.\n• Board Meeting formatting: An extra horizontal line or border appears whenever I add a line immediately after a \"Topic.\" Adding a line anywhere else works as intended.\n\nDate functionality:\n• Proposal: Could the date functionality used in the \"Board Seminar\" document also be implemented here?\n• Board Meeting: Is it possible to use the date functionality from the \"Board Seminar\" document here as well?\n\nMaster:\n• Review: Because the bullet sizes and spacing still look incorrect on my screen, we need to review them with Tariq.\n• Tables: Please provide an explanation or walkthrough showing how the tables work.\n• Color palette: The full set of currently available colors should not all be offered as options."
  },
